{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2169-11-12 16:48:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hello, I'm Dr. Lee. You're here today for your scheduled left lower extremity angiogram, correct?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2169-11-12 16:49:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, that's right. I’ve been waiting for this since my last hospital stay."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2169-11-12 16:50:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I see. Last time, the procedure was postponed because of kidney concerns. But now we’ve optimized your condition, so we’re going ahead today."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2169-11-12 16:51:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Good. My foot ulcer hasn’t been healing, and I’m worried about it getting worse."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2169-11-12 16:52:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s exactly why we’re doing the angiogram — to check the blood flow to your leg and foot. Poor circulation can delay healing."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2169-11-12 16:53:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Will they fix anything during the test?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2169-11-12 16:54:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Sometimes they can do both, but today the main goal is diagnosis. If there’s a blockage that can be treated, they might, but we’ll see what the images show."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2169-11-12 16:55:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay. And I heard they’re using the groin to access the artery?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2169-11-12 16:56:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, they’ll go through the right femoral artery. It’s a common approach. You’ll be sedated, so you won’t feel much."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2169-11-12 16:57:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my warfarin? I stopped it before coming, like last time."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2169-11-12 16:58:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, that was correct. We’re not giving it today, but you’ll restart it tomorrow night after we make sure there’s no bleeding risk."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2169-11-12 16:59:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Alright. And my other meds — should I take them?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2169-11-12 17:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Most will be resumed after the procedure. Things like your aspirin, statin, and torsemide. We’ll hold anything that might affect bleeding until we’re sure you’re stable."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2169-11-12 17:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, thanks. I just want to make sure everything’s covered."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2169-11-12 17:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Absolutely. We’ll monitor you closely. Any signs of pain, swelling, or numbness after the procedure, let us know right away."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2169-11-12 17:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Got it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2169-11-12 18:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi again. You did well during the angiogram. They accessed the right femoral artery and looked at the left leg’s blood vessels."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2169-11-12 18:31:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And what did they find?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2169-11-12 18:32:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "The main arteries in your thigh are open, but there are a few narrow spots that aren’t severe. The bigger issue is in the lower leg."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2169-11-12 18:33:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "What’s going on down there?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2169-11-12 18:34:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "The posterior tibial artery is completely blocked. That’s one of the two main arteries to the foot. The anterior tibial is open and reaches the forefoot, but the hindfoot isn’t getting good blood flow."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2169-11-12 18:35:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So that’s why my heel ulcer isn’t healing?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2169-11-12 18:36:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Exactly. Without enough blood, wounds can’t heal properly. Given the findings, they decided not to do any intervention today — it wouldn’t help much with the current blockage pattern."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2169-11-12 18:37:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So what now?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2169-11-12 18:38:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We focus on wound care and managing your other conditions. You’ll keep using the honey gel and ammonium lactate. Good blood sugar control is also key."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2169-11-12 18:39:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "My sugars have been hard to control with the gastroparesis."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2169-11-12 18:40:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I know. That’s why we’re continuing the sliding scale insulin. We’ll check your levels regularly and adjust as needed."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2169-11-12 18:41:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my kidneys? Last time they were worried about contrast affecting them."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2169-11-12 18:42:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good point. They used minimal contrast and took precautions. Your creatinine is 2.2, which is stable for you, so no acute kidney injury."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2169-11-12 18:43:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s a relief."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2169-11-13 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. You’re doing well. Vital signs are stable, and you’ve been eating and moving around without issues."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2169-11-13 09:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I feel okay. A little tired, but no pain."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2169-11-13 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s expected. The procedure takes energy, even if you were sedated. Your foot and groin site are looking good — no swelling or bleeding."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2169-11-13 09:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Can I go home today?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2169-11-13 09:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, we think you’re ready. You’ll go home with instructions on wound care, activity, and when to call us if something goes wrong."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2169-11-13 09:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my warfarin?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2169-11-13 09:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ll restart your 4 mg dose tonight. Just like before. Keep an eye on the groin site — if it starts bleeding or swells, lie down and press on it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2169-11-13 09:07:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And when do I follow up?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2169-11-13 09:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ll have an appointment for bilateral ABI/PVR tests to monitor blood flow. The office will call you to schedule."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2169-11-13 09:09:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, thank you. I’ll keep my foot elevated and take care of the ulcer."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2169-11-13 09:10:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Exactly. And watch for any new pain, coldness, or color changes in your leg. Call us if those happen, or if you get a fever over 101.5."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2169-11-13 09:11:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. Thanks for explaining everything."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2169-11-13 09:12:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. We’ll get your discharge papers ready, and you should be out within the hour."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 44,
      "time": "2169-11-13 10:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Just a quick check before you leave — any questions about your meds or wound care?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 45,
      "time": "2169-11-13 10:31:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "No, it’s all clear. I’ll keep using the honey gel every other day and the ammonium lactate daily."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 46,
      "time": "2169-11-13 10:32:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Perfect. And remember — no heavy lifting for a week, and don’t drive while on pain meds."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 47,
      "time": "2169-11-13 10:33:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Got it. I’ll have my daughter help with chores."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 48,
      "time": "2169-11-13 10:34:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s a good plan. Take care, and we’ll see you in follow-up."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 49,
      "time": "2169-11-13 10:35:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you, Doctor."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 50,
      "time": "2169-11-13 10:36:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. Have a safe trip home."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2169-11-12 16:48:00",
    "admission_end": "2169-11-13 17:14:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "A woman with type 1 diabetes, a history of CABG and mitral valve replacement, and chronic kidney disease was admitted for a left lower extremity angiogram due to a nonhealing foot ulcer. The procedure was performed via the right femoral artery and showed patent iliac and femoral arteries with non-significant stenoses, but occlusion of the posterior tibial artery and poor hindfoot perfusion. No intervention was performed. She tolerated the procedure well, resumed her home medications except for warfarin, which she restarted the night after discharge. She was discharged home the following day with wound care instructions, activity restrictions, and plans for outpatient vascular follow-up with ABI/PVR testing.",
    "problems": [
      "Atherosclerosis of native arteries of the extremities with ulceration",
      "Ulcer of heel and midfoot",
      "Mitral valve disorders",
      "Congestive heart failure, unspecified",
      "Atrial fibrillation",
      "Coronary atherosclerosis of unspecified type of vessel, native or graft",
      "Diabetes with renal manifestations, type I [juvenile type], not stated as uncontrolled",
      "Hypertensive chronic kidney disease, unspecified, with chronic kidney disease stage I through stage IV, or unspecified",
      "Chronic kidney disease, unspecified",
      "Long-term (current) use of anticoagulants",
      "Diabetes with ophthalmic manifestations, type I [juvenile type], not stated as uncontrolled",
      "Background diabetic retinopathy",
      "Diabetes with neurological manifestations, type I [juvenile type], not stated as uncontrolled",
      "Polyneuropathy in diabetes",
      "Gastroparesis",
